  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "plugins/omnimux-workflow/src/client/styles.js",
      "content": "`.omx-fork-mode-card` is used on focusable interactive elements (`role=\"button\"`, `tabIndex={0}`, keyboard handlers in ForkAppProjectDialog.jsx), but it sets `outline: none` without any `:focus-visible` replacement. This removes the visible focus indicator for keyboard users. Other focusable elements in this stylesheet (e.g. `.omnimux-workflow-card:focus-visible`, `.omnimux-new-project-drop:focus-visible`) define a focus-visible style. Please add an equivalent for consistency and accessibility.",
      "suggestion_code": "  transition: all 0.15s ease;\n}\n.omx-fork-mode-card:focus-visible {\n  outline: 2px solid var(--dsw-alias-brand-primary);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}",
      "existing_code": "  transition: all 0.15s ease;\n  outline: none;\n}",
      "start_line": 1968,
      "end_line": 1970,
      "category": "style",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "plugins/omnimux-workflow/src/client/projects/ForkAppProjectDialog.jsx",
      "content": "The `t` prop is declared but never used — all labels are hardcoded Chinese strings ('创建应用编辑副本', '官方预设应用为受保护模板…', '浏览目录失败，请重试', '确认并进入画布' …). The sibling `NewLocalProjectDialog` uses `t('projects.dialog.*')` for the same UI (including `t('projects.dialog.browseFailed')`), so this dialog bypasses the existing localization pipeline. Either localize the strings via `t` or drop the unused parameter to avoid a dead prop.",
      "existing_code": "  t,\n  onCancel,\n  onSubmit,\n  onBrowseDirectory,\n}) {",
      "start_line": 109,
      "end_line": 113,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "plugins/omnimux-workflow/src/client/projects/ForkAppProjectDialog.jsx",
      "content": "The two mode cards are `div` elements with `role=\"button\"` that only handle Enter/Space; the active option is conveyed exclusively via the `is-active` CSS class with no `aria-pressed`/`aria-selected`/`aria-checked`, so screen readers cannot tell which mode is selected. This is a single-select control — consider `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` (or add `aria-pressed`) to expose the state.",
      "existing_code": "                  role=\"button\"\n                  tabIndex={0}\n                  className={`omx-fork-mode-card ${mode === 'page' ? 'is-active' : ''}`}",
      "start_line": 325,
      "end_line": 327,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "plugins/omnimux-workflow/src/client/projects/ForkAppProjectDialog.jsx",
      "content": "This file duplicates a large portion of `NewLocalProjectDialog` — `CloseGlyph`/`FolderGlyph`/`FolderPlusGlyph`/`ComputerGlyph`/`ChevronGlyph`, the `loadBrowse`/`openBrowse`/`applyPickedPath` logic, and the full browse/picked/drop `sourcePane` markup are near-copies, yet here they are rebuilt with raw `\u003cbutton\u003e` + `exempt-ui01 ai-app-ui-spec` instead of the shared `ModalDialog`/`IconButton`/`Button`/`InputField`. Consider extracting the shared folder-picker pane/glyphs into a reusable component to avoid the divergence (the sibling already drifted: e.g. `path` seeding, `setConfirmedExisting`).",
      "existing_code": "+function FolderPlusGlyph({ size = 14 }) {",
      "start_line": 32,
      "end_line": 32,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "path": "plugins/omnimux-workflow/src/client/projects/ForkAppProjectDialog.jsx",
      "content": "`browseError` is only rendered inside the `mode === 'project'` branch below, but the state is not reset when the mode switches to 'page' (it is only cleared on a successful load / closing browse). If a browse attempt fails and the user then switches to 'page', the error is set but its paragraph is unmounted, so the message silently disappears and re-appears if the user switches back. Minor, but resetting `browseError` on `handleModeChange('page')` would keep state consistent.",
      "existing_code": "+          {error \u0026\u0026 (\n+            \u003cp className=\"omnimux-new-project-error omx-fork-error-text\"\u003e\n+              {error}\n+            \u003c/p\u003e\n+          )}",
      "start_line": 401,
      "end_line": 405,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "path": "plugins/omnimux-workflow/src/client/projects/AppTab.jsx",
      "content": "`handleForkSubmit` schedules `setTimeout(() =\u003e setEditNotice(null), 3500)` inside `finally`, and the timer handle is never stored or cleared. On the error path the dialog remains open (error is surfaced via `forkError`), but the notice-clearing timer still fires later; if the user starts another edit/fork operation before it fires, the stale timer can wipe the newer notice. The same untracked-timer pattern was copied from `handleEditApp`, so consider tracking/clearing the timeout (e.g. via a ref with cleanup on unmount) rather than adding another fire-and-forget timer.",
      "existing_code": "    } finally {\n      setForkBusy(false)\n      setTimeout(() =\u003e setEditNotice(null), 3500)\n    }",
      "start_line": 885,
      "end_line": 888,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
